WEBVTT

00:00:02.170 --> 00:00:27.166
Storylines Level 1 The Locks Rule by Petey One, Where Am I?

00:00:27.226 --> 00:00:32.414
Where am I?

00:00:32.474 --> 00:00:33.734
I don't know.

00:00:33.754 --> 00:00:38.606
I'm in a beautiful room in an old house.

00:00:38.666 --> 00:00:44.378
There's a bed, an expensive chair, and a beautiful table.

00:00:44.438 --> 00:00:49.729
I can't see anything from the window, only a green field.

00:00:49.789 --> 00:00:52.640
The sun is shining on the field.

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:56.742
I can hear music, quiet music.

00:00:56.802 --> 00:00:59.012
It's Mozart.

00:00:59.072 --> 00:01:01.595
Why am I here?

00:01:01.655 --> 00:01:03.668
I don't know.

00:01:03.728 --> 00:01:07.280
Oh, my head is hurting.

00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:12.122
I can't open the door and I can't open the window.

00:01:12.182 --> 00:01:16.925
I'm wearing grey trousers and a grey shirt.

00:01:16.984 --> 00:01:19.386
I'm not wearing any shoes.

00:01:19.446 --> 00:01:22.818
I'm hungry and I'm thirsty.

00:01:22.878 --> 00:01:27.881
There isn't any food in the room and there isn't a drink either.

00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:34.437
There's a pen and some paper on the table There isn't anything on the paper.

00:01:34.497 --> 00:01:36.809
Who am I?

00:01:36.869 --> 00:01:39.310
I can't remember.

00:01:39.370 --> 00:01:41.912
I can't remember my name.

00:01:41.972 --> 00:01:44.385
I can't remember anything.

00:01:44.445 --> 00:01:47.188
Oh, my head hurts a lot.

00:01:47.248 --> 00:01:49.940
I'm very tired.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:55.604
I'm going to sleep.

00:01:55.664 --> 00:02:00.328
It's morning.

00:02:00.388 --> 00:02:01.958
I'm on the bed.

00:02:02.018 --> 00:02:04.120
I'm wearing the gray clothes.

00:02:04.180 --> 00:02:07.042
I'm very hungry and very thirsty.

00:02:07.101 --> 00:02:08.843
I can hear music again.

00:02:08.903 --> 00:02:10.654
It's the Mozart again.

00:02:10.714 --> 00:02:15.688
My head doesn't hurt now, but I can't remember my name.

00:02:15.748 --> 00:02:18.470
I can't remember anything.

00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:20.852
I can hear someone.

00:02:20.912 --> 00:02:23.314
There's someone outside the room.

00:02:23.374 --> 00:02:27.026
The door is opening.

00:02:27.086 --> 00:02:30.383
He's in the room.

00:02:30.442 --> 00:02:34.621
He's wearing black trousers and a black shirt.

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:36.642
I don't know him.

00:02:36.702 --> 00:02:37.803
Hello.

00:02:37.823 --> 00:02:39.324
How's your head?

00:02:39.384 --> 00:02:40.566
My head.

00:02:40.626 --> 00:02:41.986
It's okay.

00:02:42.046 --> 00:02:43.358
It doesn't hurt now.

00:02:43.418 --> 00:02:44.148
Good.

00:02:44.208 --> 00:02:45.520
Where am I?

00:02:45.580 --> 00:02:46.781
You don't know?

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:47.692
No.

00:02:47.752 --> 00:02:49.103
Are you thirsty?

00:02:49.162 --> 00:02:49.934
Yes.

00:02:49.994 --> 00:02:51.905
I'm hungry and thirsty.

00:02:51.965 --> 00:02:53.967
Drink this.

00:02:54.027 --> 00:02:57.120
He's got a glass in his hand.

00:02:57.180 --> 00:03:01.864
I drink from the glass.

00:03:01.924 --> 00:03:07.030
I'm very tired again.

00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:11.224
I'm going to sleep.

00:03:11.283 --> 00:03:15.097
What time is it?

00:03:15.156 --> 00:03:18.160
My head's hurting again.

00:03:18.219 --> 00:03:21.602
I'm on the bed and the room is dark.

00:03:21.662 --> 00:03:23.944
I can't hear music now.

00:03:24.004 --> 00:03:26.546
I'm going to turn on the light.

00:03:26.606 --> 00:03:28.889
Now I can see.

00:03:28.948 --> 00:03:31.610
There's a glass on the table.

00:03:31.670 --> 00:03:33.781
I'm thirsty again.

00:03:33.841 --> 00:03:39.062
I'm going to drink from the glass.

00:03:39.122 --> 00:03:44.345
Sleep.

00:03:44.405 --> 00:03:47.716
I'm going to sleep.

00:03:47.776 --> 00:03:49.187
Wake up.

00:03:49.247 --> 00:03:50.258
What?

00:03:50.318 --> 00:03:51.799
Oh, my head.

00:03:51.859 --> 00:03:53.780
I'm going to ask you some questions.

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:54.860
Who are you?

00:03:54.920 --> 00:03:55.680
I don't know.

00:03:55.740 --> 00:03:56.461
What's your name?

00:03:56.481 --> 00:03:57.321
I don't know.

00:03:57.341 --> 00:03:58.522
I'm going to ask you again.

00:03:58.582 --> 00:03:59.492
What's your name?

00:03:59.552 --> 00:04:00.583
I can't tell you.

00:04:00.643 --> 00:04:01.363
I don't know.

00:04:01.383 --> 00:04:02.814
Where are you from?

00:04:02.873 --> 00:04:03.903
I don't know.

00:04:03.963 --> 00:04:04.593
Drink this.

00:04:04.653 --> 00:04:05.304
No.

00:04:05.364 --> 00:04:06.324
I can't.

00:04:06.384 --> 00:04:07.714
You're going to drink it.

00:04:07.774 --> 00:04:09.754
Do you understand?

00:04:09.814 --> 00:04:12.435
There's a gun in his head.

00:04:12.495 --> 00:04:15.706
I drink from the glass.

00:04:15.766 --> 00:04:20.688
The room is dark.

00:04:20.748 --> 00:04:29.350
Two questions.

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:32.418
I'm awake again.

00:04:32.478 --> 00:04:34.438
It's quite outside.

00:04:34.498 --> 00:04:37.230
The sun is shining outside the window.

00:04:37.290 --> 00:04:39.982
There's food and water on the table.

00:04:40.042 --> 00:04:41.783
I'm not tired now.

00:04:41.843 --> 00:04:43.674
And my head's okay.

00:04:43.734 --> 00:04:45.726
Someone's coming.

00:04:45.786 --> 00:04:48.638
The door opens.

00:04:48.698 --> 00:04:52.321
It's the man in black clothes.

00:04:52.380 --> 00:04:54.192
You want to talk though?

00:04:54.252 --> 00:04:55.474
What about?

00:04:55.534 --> 00:04:56.734
Okay.

00:04:56.794 --> 00:04:57.785
Who are you?

00:04:57.845 --> 00:04:58.676
Who are you?

00:04:58.736 --> 00:04:59.866
I'm asking the questions.

00:04:59.906 --> 00:05:00.817
Why are you here?

00:05:00.877 --> 00:05:03.616
You tell me.

00:05:03.676 --> 00:05:06.645
Then he hits me.

00:05:06.705 --> 00:05:08.225
He hits me across the face.

00:05:08.245 --> 00:05:10.047
We're going to start again.

00:05:10.106 --> 00:05:11.277
Who are you?

00:05:11.337 --> 00:05:12.567
I can't remember.

00:05:12.627 --> 00:05:14.498
Well, don't hit me.

00:05:14.558 --> 00:05:17.200
But he does.

00:05:17.260 --> 00:05:21.912
Then he opens the door and he goes.

00:05:21.972 --> 00:05:25.403
There's a bump on the back of my head.

00:05:25.463 --> 00:05:29.244
It doesn't hurt now, but my face hurts.

00:05:29.304 --> 00:05:31.333
A bump.

00:05:31.393 --> 00:05:34.272
I can remember something.

00:05:34.332 --> 00:05:36.902
I can remember.

00:05:36.962 --> 00:05:39.132
I'm in a field.

00:05:39.192 --> 00:05:42.204
I'm lying under a tree.

00:05:42.263 --> 00:05:45.864
I've got some binoculars in my hand.

00:05:45.924 --> 00:05:48.315
I'm watching a house.

00:05:48.375 --> 00:05:51.676
It's a beautiful old house.

00:05:51.736 --> 00:05:55.607
Then there's a noise behind me.

00:05:55.666 --> 00:05:59.718
It's a man with a dog, a big dog.

00:05:59.778 --> 00:06:02.560
The man's holding a gun.

00:06:02.620 --> 00:06:05.044
Then the man's hitting me.

00:06:05.104 --> 00:06:08.286
He's hitting me on the head with the gun.

00:06:08.346 --> 00:06:11.468
Then everything's going dark.

00:06:11.528 --> 00:06:14.921
I've got a bump on my head now.

00:06:14.981 --> 00:06:17.042
Why?

00:06:17.102 --> 00:06:18.904
Why am I in that field?

00:06:18.964 --> 00:06:20.576
Who am I?

00:06:20.636 --> 00:06:22.757
Am I a policeman?

00:06:22.817 --> 00:06:24.638
Am I a spy?

00:06:24.698 --> 00:06:26.200
And who is the man?

00:06:26.260 --> 00:06:27.401
Is he a policeman?

00:06:27.461 --> 00:06:29.032
Is he a spy?

00:06:29.092 --> 00:06:31.114
Or is he a criminal?

00:06:31.174 --> 00:06:33.612
I don't know.

00:06:33.672 --> 00:06:36.728
But now I can remember something.

00:06:36.788 --> 00:06:38.169
Tomorrow.

00:06:38.229 --> 00:06:41.189
Tomorrow, I'm going to remember some more.

00:06:41.249 --> 00:06:41.979
Three.

00:06:42.039 --> 00:06:53.678
No more time.

00:06:53.738 --> 00:07:09.059
The next day, the man with black clothes is in the room again.

00:07:09.119 --> 00:07:11.441
Well, how are you today?

00:07:11.461 --> 00:07:12.612
I'm OK.

00:07:12.672 --> 00:07:13.813
Can you remember anything?

00:07:13.873 --> 00:07:15.064
Yes, a little.

00:07:15.124 --> 00:07:16.535
Who are you working for?

00:07:16.595 --> 00:07:17.626
I don't know.

00:07:17.686 --> 00:07:19.117
Why are you watching us?

00:07:19.177 --> 00:07:20.348
I don't know.

00:07:20.408 --> 00:07:21.710
Who are you?

00:07:21.770 --> 00:07:22.700
Tell me.

00:07:22.760 --> 00:07:24.992
Then, maybe I can remember.

00:07:25.052 --> 00:07:26.244
Very clever.

00:07:26.304 --> 00:07:28.134
I can't tell you anything.

00:07:28.194 --> 00:07:30.807
He goes out.

00:07:30.867 --> 00:07:33.873
I remember again.

00:07:33.933 --> 00:07:35.958
I'm watching the house.

00:07:36.018 --> 00:07:37.440
It's evening.

00:07:37.499 --> 00:07:40.072
I'm wearing a blue coat.

00:07:40.132 --> 00:07:42.333
There are lights in the house.

00:07:42.393 --> 00:07:44.985
The car's going to the house.

00:07:45.045 --> 00:07:47.306
It's a white Jaguar.

00:07:47.366 --> 00:07:49.328
I'm watching carefully.

00:07:49.388 --> 00:07:51.850
I can see two people.

00:07:51.910 --> 00:07:53.952
They've got a box.

00:07:54.012 --> 00:08:01.378
Then, then there's the noise behind me and the bump on the head.

00:08:01.438 --> 00:08:03.627
It's dark.

00:08:03.687 --> 00:08:06.026
I can hear voices outside the room.

00:08:06.086 --> 00:08:07.918
Well, he's going to talk.

00:08:07.978 --> 00:08:08.689
Maybe.

00:08:08.749 --> 00:08:10.931
He can't remember anything because of the bump on his head.

00:08:10.991 --> 00:08:12.152
What about the drinks?

00:08:12.212 --> 00:08:13.894
No, the drinks aren't helping us.

00:08:13.953 --> 00:08:14.874
Okay.

00:08:14.934 --> 00:08:16.296
Two days more.

00:08:16.356 --> 00:08:17.567
Then that's it.

00:08:17.627 --> 00:08:19.648
We haven't got any more time.

00:08:19.708 --> 00:08:21.160
How much does he know?

00:08:21.220 --> 00:08:26.244
That's the important thing.

00:08:26.304 --> 00:08:31.008
Four.

00:08:31.068 --> 00:08:35.051
Out of the locked room.

00:08:35.110 --> 00:08:38.632
I hear a key.

00:08:38.692 --> 00:08:41.113
They're putting a key into the lock.

00:08:41.174 --> 00:08:43.775
They're turning the key.

00:08:43.836 --> 00:08:46.668
They're locking the door.

00:08:46.728 --> 00:08:48.919
They're walking away.

00:08:48.979 --> 00:08:51.670
But the key is in the lock.

00:08:51.730 --> 00:08:53.682
Two days more.

00:08:53.742 --> 00:08:54.723
And that's it.

00:08:54.783 --> 00:08:56.064
What are they going to do?

00:08:56.084 --> 00:08:58.576
I can't stay here.

00:08:58.636 --> 00:09:01.788
The key is in the lock.

00:09:01.848 --> 00:09:05.440
I've got some paper from the table.

00:09:05.500 --> 00:09:06.915
Now.

00:09:06.975 --> 00:09:09.150
Put the paper floor.

00:09:09.210 --> 00:09:12.120
Push the paper under the door.

00:09:12.180 --> 00:09:15.521
The papers under the door.

00:09:15.581 --> 00:09:18.482
Now, take the pen.

00:09:18.542 --> 00:09:22.673
Push the pen into the lock.

00:09:22.733 --> 00:09:24.864
Yes, there's the key.

00:09:24.924 --> 00:09:26.564
It is in the lock.

00:09:26.624 --> 00:09:29.395
Push the key with the pen.

00:09:29.455 --> 00:09:33.566
Yes, the key is falling from the lock.

00:09:33.626 --> 00:09:35.296
Is it on the paper?

00:09:35.356 --> 00:09:37.432
Oh, I don't know.

00:09:37.492 --> 00:09:40.230
Pull the paper under the door.

00:09:40.290 --> 00:09:43.962
Pull it slowly and carefully.

00:09:44.022 --> 00:09:49.096
Very slowly and very carefully.

00:09:49.156 --> 00:09:51.868
It's coming under the door.

00:09:51.928 --> 00:09:53.710
And there's the key.

00:09:53.770 --> 00:09:55.262
It's on the paper.

00:09:55.322 --> 00:09:56.952
I've got the key.

00:09:57.012 --> 00:09:59.355
I can open the door.

00:09:59.415 --> 00:10:02.067
It's quiet outside.

00:10:02.127 --> 00:10:07.180
I'm opening the door very quietly and carefully.

00:10:07.240 --> 00:10:10.091
There's a corridor.

00:10:10.151 --> 00:10:11.792
It's empty.

00:10:11.852 --> 00:10:13.654
I'm going out.

00:10:13.714 --> 00:10:18.977
Now I'm going to take the key.

00:10:19.037 --> 00:10:23.290
I'm walking along the corridor.

00:10:23.349 --> 00:10:25.472
It's a beautiful house.

00:10:25.532 --> 00:10:28.664
I can hear the music again, the Mozart.

00:10:28.724 --> 00:10:31.034
There are a lot of doors.

00:10:31.094 --> 00:10:34.658
At the end, I can see stairs.

00:10:34.718 --> 00:10:37.463
I can hear people downstairs.

00:10:37.523 --> 00:10:39.728
I can't go down.

00:10:39.788 --> 00:10:42.478
I open some doors.

00:10:42.538 --> 00:10:44.759
There are bedrooms.

00:10:44.819 --> 00:10:47.400
I open four or five doors.

00:10:47.460 --> 00:10:50.471
Then I open another door.

00:10:50.531 --> 00:10:54.152
The room is full of paintings, things.

00:10:54.212 --> 00:10:59.374
Picasso's, Rembrandt's, Van Gogh, they're beautiful.

00:10:59.434 --> 00:11:00.964
They're on the floor.

00:11:01.024 --> 00:11:03.015
Millions of pounds in this room.

00:11:03.075 --> 00:11:04.396
Millions.

00:11:04.456 --> 00:11:06.708
I look at a Picasso.

00:11:06.768 --> 00:11:11.214
It's the famous stolen Picasso from the London Art Gallery.

00:11:11.274 --> 00:11:13.266
Who are they?

00:11:13.326 --> 00:11:15.637
There are thieves.

00:11:15.698 --> 00:11:18.190
But who am I?

00:11:18.250 --> 00:11:21.922
I closed the door.

00:11:21.983 --> 00:11:25.766
How can I get out of this house?

00:11:25.826 --> 00:11:28.598
They have got guns.

00:11:28.658 --> 00:11:32.491
I remember one of the bedrooms.

00:11:32.551 --> 00:11:34.312
There's a telephone.

00:11:34.372 --> 00:11:36.953
I can telephone the police.

00:11:37.013 --> 00:11:41.674
I walk quickly along the corridor and open the door.

00:11:41.734 --> 00:11:45.097
The telephone is next to the bed.

00:11:45.157 --> 00:11:47.618
The number is on the telephone.

00:11:47.678 --> 00:11:51.262
Bradstreet, 35972.

00:11:51.322 --> 00:11:54.123
I take the telephone carefully.

00:11:54.183 --> 00:11:55.394
999.

00:11:55.454 --> 00:12:01.258
I'm waiting.

00:12:01.318 --> 00:12:04.780
Please fire our ambulance.

00:12:04.840 --> 00:12:07.259
Please, quickly.

00:12:07.319 --> 00:12:09.478
Police.

00:12:09.538 --> 00:12:10.798
What's your number?

00:12:10.858 --> 00:12:13.531
Bradstreet 35972.

00:12:13.591 --> 00:12:14.522
Quickly.

00:12:14.582 --> 00:12:15.812
I'm a prisoner here.

00:12:15.872 --> 00:12:17.154
I can't get out.

00:12:17.214 --> 00:12:19.496
The house is full of stolen paintings.

00:12:19.556 --> 00:12:20.876
Come quickly.

00:12:20.936 --> 00:12:22.178
What's your name?

00:12:22.238 --> 00:12:23.558
Come quickly.

00:12:23.618 --> 00:12:25.440
This is Bradstreet 35972.

00:12:25.500 --> 00:12:28.342
I can't...

00:12:28.402 --> 00:12:31.505
Then I hear people in the corridor.

00:12:31.565 --> 00:12:33.276
I put down the phone.

00:12:33.336 --> 00:12:35.944
I can hear them outside the locked room.

00:12:36.004 --> 00:12:38.051
We'll open the door then.

00:12:38.111 --> 00:12:39.352
I can't find the key.

00:12:39.412 --> 00:12:40.113
Come on.

00:12:40.133 --> 00:12:41.004
I can't find it.

00:12:41.064 --> 00:12:42.595
There's another key in the kitchen.

00:12:42.635 --> 00:12:43.305
Get it.

00:12:43.366 --> 00:12:47.479
Right.

00:12:47.539 --> 00:12:52.142
Bye.

00:12:52.202 --> 00:12:56.536
Who am I?

00:12:56.596 --> 00:13:00.379
Five minutes.

00:13:00.439 --> 00:13:02.070
I can hear him again.

00:13:02.130 --> 00:13:04.022
He's coming with the key.

00:13:04.082 --> 00:13:06.770
He's out in the door.

00:13:06.830 --> 00:13:08.958
What?

00:13:09.018 --> 00:13:10.528
He isn't here.

00:13:10.588 --> 00:13:11.548
What?

00:13:11.608 --> 00:13:13.109
But the doors locked.

00:13:13.169 --> 00:13:15.410
Find him and take your gun.

00:13:15.470 --> 00:13:17.371
And this time, finish him.

00:13:17.431 --> 00:13:18.471
You understand?

00:13:18.531 --> 00:13:20.552
Okay, I'm going.

00:13:20.612 --> 00:13:22.793
I can hear him.

00:13:22.853 --> 00:13:24.814
He's opening doors.

00:13:24.874 --> 00:13:27.796
Are the police going to come or not?

00:13:27.856 --> 00:13:30.316
He's in the next room.

00:13:30.376 --> 00:13:32.417
Then I hear them.

00:13:32.477 --> 00:13:34.828
Police cars, a lot of police cars.

00:13:34.888 --> 00:13:36.610
They're outside the house.

00:13:36.670 --> 00:13:38.090
It's the police.

00:13:38.150 --> 00:13:39.501
What do they want?

00:13:39.561 --> 00:13:41.692
Don't take the gun with you.

00:13:41.752 --> 00:13:43.583
They're going downstairs.

00:13:43.643 --> 00:13:46.344
I can hear voices.

00:13:46.404 --> 00:13:49.456
Good evening, Inspector.

00:13:49.516 --> 00:13:51.487
What can I do for you?

00:13:51.547 --> 00:13:53.928
We want to look around the house.

00:13:53.988 --> 00:13:56.109
We're looking for some paintings.

00:13:56.169 --> 00:13:57.900
But there's nothing here.

00:13:57.960 --> 00:13:59.020
Nothing.

00:13:59.080 --> 00:14:00.481
We can look then.

00:14:00.541 --> 00:14:01.371
But why?

00:14:01.391 --> 00:14:03.482
A telephone call.

00:14:03.542 --> 00:14:06.124
A telephone call about some paintings.

00:14:06.184 --> 00:14:07.073
From?

00:14:07.133 --> 00:14:08.763
We don't know.

00:14:08.823 --> 00:14:11.665
You don't know well.

00:14:11.725 --> 00:14:13.286
The paintings are up here.

00:14:13.346 --> 00:14:14.347
I can show you.

00:14:14.407 --> 00:14:15.798
Follow me.

00:14:15.858 --> 00:14:18.350
It's 10 minutes later.

00:14:18.410 --> 00:14:21.552
The man and the woman are in the police cars.

00:14:21.612 --> 00:14:24.804
Well, Eddie, this is a surprise.

00:14:24.864 --> 00:14:27.096
Eddie, is that my name?

00:14:27.156 --> 00:14:29.838
Eddie, come on.

00:14:29.898 --> 00:14:31.499
No, I can't remember.

00:14:31.559 --> 00:14:33.420
You can't remember me.

00:14:33.480 --> 00:14:35.192
I can't remember my name.

00:14:35.252 --> 00:14:37.630
Eddie, Eddie what?

00:14:37.690 --> 00:14:39.800
Eddie Hampton.

00:14:39.860 --> 00:14:42.321
What are you doing here, Eddie?

00:14:42.381 --> 00:14:43.562
I tell him.

00:14:43.622 --> 00:14:46.404
I tell him about the field and the binoculars.

00:14:46.464 --> 00:14:49.856
I tell him about the bump on my head and the room.

00:14:49.916 --> 00:14:53.048
I tell him about the paper and the key.

00:14:53.108 --> 00:14:56.120
He's laughing at me.

00:14:56.180 --> 00:15:00.944
Okay, I'm Eddie Hampton, but who's Eddie Hampton?

00:15:01.004 --> 00:15:03.586
He's laughing again.

00:15:03.646 --> 00:15:05.176
You know me.

00:15:05.236 --> 00:15:06.810
Am I a policeman?

00:15:06.870 --> 00:15:08.204
No Eddie.

00:15:08.264 --> 00:15:10.166
You aren't a policeman.

00:15:10.226 --> 00:15:11.587
Then who am I?

00:15:11.647 --> 00:15:13.418
And what am I doing here?

00:15:13.478 --> 00:15:14.949
I don't know.

00:15:15.009 --> 00:15:17.030
But I can't tell you something.

00:15:17.090 --> 00:15:18.000
What?

00:15:18.060 --> 00:15:20.442
Eddie Hampton's a criminal.

00:15:20.502 --> 00:15:21.763
A thief.

00:15:21.823 --> 00:15:23.594
Not a big thief.

00:15:23.654 --> 00:15:28.437
Those two people are big thieves with their famous paintings.

00:15:28.497 --> 00:15:31.429
No, you're a small thief Eddie.

00:15:31.489 --> 00:15:33.415
You steal from houses.

00:15:33.475 --> 00:15:39.716
televisions, radios, videos, high-fives, a little money sometimes.

00:15:39.776 --> 00:15:52.743
You're a small but thank you for your help.

